<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<Defs>
  <!-- Formation flag: the cores use the flags around them to mark the area (convex polygon). Stuff decides element via feng shui. -->
  <ThingDef ParentName="BuildingBase">
    <defName>CVG_FormationFlag</defName>
    <label>formation flag</label>
    <description>A tall flag on a stake, inscribed with runes. Place at least three around a formation core (within 16 cells): the area enclosed by the flags is where the formation works. More flags raise its level. The first formation masters of Jiuxiao planted red flags on the corners of a field to tell the land where one qi ended and another began. Sect disciples still sew each rune by hand, because a flag stitched in a hurry lets the formation breathe out.</description>
    <graphicData>
      <texPath>Things/Building/CVG/Formations/FormationFlag</texPath>
      <graphicClass>Graphic_Single</graphicClass><drawRotated>false</drawRotated>
      <drawSize>(1.3,1.3)</drawSize>
    </graphicData>
    <category>Building</category>
    <altitudeLayer>Building</altitudeLayer>
    <passability>PassThroughOnly</passability>
    <pathCost>14</pathCost>
    <fillPercent>0.1</fillPercent>
    <rotatable>false</rotatable>
    <selectable>true</selectable>
    <designationCategory>CVG_Formations</designationCategory>
    <uiOrder>2520</uiOrder>
    <statBases>
      <MaxHitPoints>80</MaxHitPoints>
      <WorkToBuild>400</WorkToBuild>
      <Flammability>1.0</Flammability>
      <Beauty>1</Beauty>
    </statBases>
    <costList>
      <WoodLog>10</WoodLog>
      <Cloth>5</Cloth>
      <CVG_SpiritStone>1</CVG_SpiritStone>
    </costList>
    <researchPrerequisites><li>CVG_Research_FiveElements</li></researchPrerequisites>
    <modExtensions>
      <li Class="Convergence.DefModExtension_FengShui">
        <qi>1</qi>
      </li>
    </modExtensions>
    <placeWorkers><li>Convergence.Formations.PlaceWorker_FormationRange</li></placeWorkers>
  </ThingDef>

  <ThingDef ParentName="BuildingBase">
    <defName>CVG_QiGatheringCore</defName>
    <label>qi gathering formation core</label>
    <description>The heart of a Qi Gathering Formation. Burns spirit stones slowly and, with flags enclosing an area, raises the qi concentration of every cell inside (+1 per level), indoors or outdoors. Formless Sword records say the Gathering Array was drawn by a sword saint who was tired of chasing qi across mountains and decided to make the mountain come to him. Its stone brazier never smokes, but the air around it tastes of rain. Formation flags are in the Security tab.</description>
    <graphicData>
      <texPath>Things/Building/CVG/Formations/QiGatheringCore</texPath>
      <graphicClass>Graphic_Single</graphicClass>
      <drawRotated>false</drawRotated>
      <drawSize>(1.3,1.3)</drawSize>
    </graphicData>
    <category>Building</category>
    <altitudeLayer>Building</altitudeLayer>
    <passability>PassThroughOnly</passability>
    <pathCost>30</pathCost>
    <fillPercent>0.3</fillPercent>
    <rotatable>false</rotatable>
    <tickerType>Normal</tickerType>
    <selectable>true</selectable>
    <designationCategory>CVG_Formations</designationCategory>
    <uiOrder>2530</uiOrder>
    <statBases>
      <MaxHitPoints>180</MaxHitPoints>
      <WorkToBuild>2500</WorkToBuild>
      <Flammability>0.3</Flammability>
      <Beauty>2</Beauty>
      <MeditationFocusStrength>0.0</MeditationFocusStrength>
    </statBases>
    <costList>
      <CVG_SpiritStone>10</CVG_SpiritStone>
      <WoodLog>30</WoodLog>
    </costList>
    <researchPrerequisites><li>CVG_Research_QiGathering</li></researchPrerequisites>
    <comps>
      <li Class="CompProperties_Refuelable">
        <fuelConsumptionRate>0.4</fuelConsumptionRate>
        <fuelCapacity>20</fuelCapacity>
        <fuelFilter><thingDefs><li>CVG_SpiritStone</li></thingDefs></fuelFilter>
        <initialFuelPercent>0.5</initialFuelPercent>
        <consumeFuelOnlyWhenUsed>true</consumeFuelOnlyWhenUsed>
        <showAllowAutoRefuelToggle>true</showAllowAutoRefuelToggle>
        <autoRefuelPercent>0.4</autoRefuelPercent>
        <fuelLabel>Spirit stones</fuelLabel>
        <fuelGizmoLabel>Spirit stones</fuelGizmoLabel>
      </li>
      <li Class="Convergence.Formations.CompProperties_FormationCore">
        <workerClass>Convergence.Formations.FormationWorker_QiGather</workerClass>
        <flagDef>CVG_FormationFlag</flagDef>
        <minFlags>3</minFlags>
        <maxLinkRange>15.9</maxLinkRange>
        <maxCells>600</maxCells>
        <power>1</power>
        <intervalTicks>240</intervalTicks>
        <fuelPerEvent>0</fuelPerEvent>
        <color>(0.45,0.9,0.6)</color>
      </li>
      <li Class="CompProperties_Glower"><glowRadius>5</glowRadius><glowColor>(120,180,255,0)</glowColor></li>
    </comps>
    <placeWorkers><li>PlaceWorker_GlowRadius</li><li>Convergence.Formations.PlaceWorker_FormationRange</li></placeWorkers>
    <modExtensions>
      <li Class="Convergence.DefModExtension_ProgressCounter"><counter>Formations</counter><amount>3</amount></li>
    </modExtensions>
  </ThingDef>

  <ThingDef ParentName="BuildingBase">
    <defName>CVG_SwordFormationCore</defName>
    <label>killing swords formation core</label>
    <description>Core of the Formation of Killing Swords. Every two seconds it launches qi swords (one per level) at the enemies inside the flags' area. Each volley uses a little spirit stone. The Formation of Killing Swords is the oldest defense of the Formless Sword Sect: ten thousand swords sleeping in the Sword Graveyard answer the call of a single core. Elders warn that the swords do not tell friend from foe, only the array's edge.</description>
